<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sambhupura</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sambhupura was a city of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a>, at or near present-day Sambor in Kratié Province. Known from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> inscriptions, it was the seat of a local dynasty in the 8th century, after Chenla had broken up into rival principalities, and it remained a religious centre in the Angkorian period.</p></div>
